abstract:
GNAO1 (OMIM 139311) encodes an Gα0 CNS protein responsible for regulation&#13;
of GABA-B and α2-receptors, and neurotransmitter release. Mutations of GNAO1 are reported in patients with epileptic encephalopathy (EE) at times with a movement disorder (MD); some display severe hyperkinetic movements&#13;
without EE, three underwent Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS) with reduction in&#13;
exacerbations.1–4 (see online supplementary table 3, supporting information (SI)).
